<article class="env-definition" id="05HZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05HZ">Definition <span data-tag="05HZ">38.6.4</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a finite type ring map. Let $\mathfrak q$ be a prime of $S$ lying over the prime $\mathfrak r$ of $R$. Let $N$ be a finite $S$-module. A <em>complete dévissage of $N/S/R$ at $\mathfrak q$</em> is given by a complete dévissage $(A_ i, B_ i, M_ i, \alpha _ i)_{i = 1, \ldots , n}$ of $N/S/R$ over $\mathfrak r$ and prime ideals $\mathfrak q_ i \subset B_ i$ lying over $\mathfrak r$ such that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\kappa (\mathfrak r) \subset \kappa (\mathfrak q_ i)$ is purely transcendental, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
there is a unique prime $\mathfrak q'_ i \subset A_ i$ lying over $\mathfrak q_ i \subset B_ i$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathfrak q = \mathfrak q'_1 \cap S$ and $\mathfrak q_ i = \mathfrak q'_{i + 1} \cap A_ i$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R \to B_ i$ has relative dimension $\dim _{\mathfrak q_ i}(\text{Supp}(M_ i \otimes _ R \kappa (\mathfrak r)))$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>